{"text": "Okay, so I need to make 24 using the numbers 1, 11, 12, and 12.", "start": 0, "end": 63, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Each number has to be used exactly once, and I can use addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.", "start": 64, "end": 171, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Hmm, let's see.", "start": 172, "end": 187, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "First, I should list out all the numbers: 1, 11, 12, 12.", "start": 189, "end": 245, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Since there are two 12s, maybe that can help.", "start": 246, "end": 291, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me think about possible combinations.", "start": 292, "end": 333, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "24 is a multiple of 12, so maybe if I can get 2 from the other numbers, then 12 by 2 would be 24.", "start": 335, "end": 432, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But the other numbers are 1 and 11.", "start": 433, "end": 468, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "How can I get 2 from 1 and 11?", "start": 469, "end": 499, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "11 minus 1 is 10, which is too big.", "start": 500, "end": 535, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1 minus 11 is negative 10.", "start": 536, "end": 562, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "That's not helpful.", "start": 563, "end": 582, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Maybe division?", "start": 583, "end": 598, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "11 divided by 1 is 11, which doesn't help.", "start": 599, "end": 641, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Hmm.", "start": 642, "end": 646, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "Alternatively, maybe 12 divided by something.", "start": 648, "end": 693, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "If I take 12 divided by (something) to get a number that can multiply with another 12.", "start": 694, "end": 780, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Wait, 12 divided by (12 - 11) would be 12 divided by 1, which is 12.", "start": 781, "end": 849, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 12 times 1 is 12, but that's not 24.", "start": 850, "end": 891, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Wait, but maybe 12 divided by (12/(11-1))?", "start": 892, "end": 934, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "Let's see: 11 minus 1 is 10.", "start": 935, "end": 963, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "Then 12 divided by 10 is 1.2, and then 12 divided by 1.2 is 10.", "start": 964, "end": 1027, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "That's not helpful.", "start": 1028, "end": 1047, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another approach: Maybe combine 12s first.", "start": 1049, "end": 1091, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "12 + 12 is 24, but then I still have 1 and 11 left.", "start": 1092, "end": 1143, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "If I subtract them?", "start": 1144, "end": 1163, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "24 - 11 -1 = 12.", "start": 1164, "end": 1180, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not helpful.", "start": 1181, "end": 1193, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "If I multiply them: 24 - (11*1) = 13.", "start": 1194, "end": 1231, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not 24.", "start": 1232, "end": 1239, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Wait, maybe use multiplication and division.", "start": 1241, "end": 1285, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "Let's see: 12 * (12 / (11 - 1)).", "start": 1286, "end": 1318, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "Let's check that.", "start": 1319, "end": 1336, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "First, 11 - 1 is 10.", "start": 1338, "end": 1358, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 12 divided by 10 is 1.2.", "start": 1359, "end": 1388, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 12 multiplied by 1.2 is 14.4.", "start": 1389, "end": 1423, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not 24.", "start": 1424, "end": 1431, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Close, but not quite.", "start": 1432, "end": 1453, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "What if I do (12 + 12) * (11 - 1).", "start": 1455, "end": 1489, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "Wait, 12 +12 is 24, 11 -1 is 10.", "start": 1490, "end": 1522, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "24 *10 is 240.", "start": 1523, "end": 1537, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "That's way too big.", "start": 1538, "end": 1557, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Alternatively, (12 - 12) is 0, which probably isn't helpful.", "start": 1559, "end": 1619, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "How about 11 + 12 + 12 -1.", "start": 1621, "end": 1647, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "That's 11 +12 is 23, plus 12 is 35, minus 1 is 34.", "start": 1648, "end": 1698, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Nope.", "start": 1699, "end": 1704, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Wait, maybe division.", "start": 1706, "end": 1727, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "Let's see: 12 * ( (12 - 11) + 1 ).", "start": 1728, "end": 1762, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "So 12 -11 is 1, plus 1 is 2.", "start": 1763, "end": 1791, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 12 *2 is 24.", "start": 1792, "end": 1809, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Oh! Wait, that uses all numbers?", "start": 1810, "end": 1842, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "Let's check:", "start": 1843, "end": 1855, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "12 * ( (12 - 11) + 1 )", "start": 1857, "end": 1879, "label": "none"}
{"text": "Breaking it down:", "start": 1881, "end": 1898, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "First, 12 -11 =1.", "start": 1900, "end": 1917, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 1 +1 =2.", "start": 1918, "end": 1931, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 12 *2=24.", "start": 1932, "end": 1946, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But wait, the numbers used are 12, 12, 11, and 1.", "start": 1947, "end": 1996, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Each exactly once.", "start": 1997, "end": 2015, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Yes! So that works.", "start": 2016, "end": 2035, "label": "confirm"}
{"text": "So the expression is 12 * (12 - 11 + 1).", "start": 2037, "end": 2077, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me verify the order of operations.", "start": 2078, "end": 2116, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Inside the parentheses: 12 -11 is 1, then 1 +1 is 2.", "start": 2117, "end": 2169, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 12 *2 is 24.", "start": 2170, "end": 2187, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perfect.", "start": 2188, "end": 2196, "label": "autoPositive"}
{"text": "Alternatively, written as 12 * ( (12 +1) -11 ).", "start": 2198, "end": 2245, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's see: 12 +1 is 13, 13 -11 is 2.", "start": 2246, "end": 2282, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "Then 12 *2=24.", "start": 2283, "end": 2297, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "That also works.", "start": 2298, "end": 2314, "label": "confirm"}
{"text": "So either way.", "start": 2315, "end": 2329, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So the solution is 12 multiplied by the sum of (12 minus 11 plus 1), which equals 24.", "start": 2331, "end": 2416, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think that's the answer.", "start": 2418, "end": 2444, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me check if there's another way, but this seems to work.", "start": 2445, "end": 2505, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me confirm again:", "start": 2506, "end": 2527, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Numbers used: 12, 12, 11, 1.", "start": 2529, "end": 2557, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Wait, no, the numbers are 1, 11, 12, 12.", "start": 2558, "end": 2598, "label": "correction"}
{"text": "So in the expression 12 * (12 - 11 +1), each number is used once.", "start": 2599, "end": 2664, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "12, 12, 11, and 1.", "start": 2665, "end": 2683, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Yes, each exactly once.", "start": 2684, "end": 2707, "label": "confirm"}
{"text": "So that's correct.", "start": 2708, "end": 2726, "label": "confirm"}
